WEBVTT

00:00.760 --> 00:02.970
<b>It is nice to see you, Sly Fox-sama.</b>

00:03.270 --> 00:08.190
<b>Oh, come on. Do you think you can just add
"sama" to anything and it'll sound polite?</b>

00:08.190 --> 00:10.160
<b>What exactly do you want today?</b>

00:10.490 --> 00:12.570
<b>Frosty as always, I see.</b>

00:12.570 --> 00:14.530
<b>I wanted to talk to you about something.</b>

00:15.160 --> 00:17.520
<b>Shirayuki, I have a question for you.</b>

00:17.860 --> 00:22.910
<b>Your master, Shinohara Hiroto,
has played four games so far.</b>

00:22.910 --> 00:25.040
<b>What rank do you think he is right now?</b>

00:25.520 --> 00:29.270
<b>He cannot gain stars while 
pretending to be a Seven Star,</b>

00:29.270 --> 00:31.040
<b>so isn't he only a One Star?</b>

00:32.030 --> 00:33.150
<b>Wrong.</b>

00:33.150 --> 00:36.990
<b>Shinohara Hiroto's actual rank is Two Star.</b>

00:37.820 --> 00:39.060
<b>Why is that?</b>

00:39.060 --> 00:42.120
<b>You know how the Unique Stars work, correct?</b>

00:42.120 --> 00:47.440
<b>When the holder of a Unique Star loses 
a game, that star is always taken from them.</b>

00:47.440 --> 00:48.050
<b>Yes.</b>

00:48.370 --> 00:55.500
<b>In the last game, he defeated the holder of 
the Indigo Star: the Phoenix, Kugasaki Seiran.</b>

00:55.860 --> 00:59.940
<b>Shinohara is a false Seven Star. 
He cannot gain any more stars.</b>

00:59.940 --> 01:04.720
<b>Yet he was still required to take the 
Indigo Unique Star that Kugasaki held.</b>

01:04.720 --> 01:09.580
<b>In a case like that, a normal star would 
usually be replaced by the Unique Star.</b>

01:09.580 --> 01:11.580
<b>I see. Which means...</b>

01:11.860 --> 01:15.080
<b>Exactly. In Shinohara's case, 
that wasn't possible.</b>

01:15.960 --> 01:20.090
<b>He already held one colored Star. 
He didn't have any normal Stars.</b>

01:20.360 --> 01:25.590
<b>In a very unusual case like that, 
the winner receives an extra Unique Star.</b>

01:25.590 --> 01:30.320
<b>So Shinohara is now "double-colored."
He has the Red Star and the Indigo Star.</b>

01:29.150 --> 01:30.560
<b>Shinohara Hiroto</b>

01:30.320 --> 01:33.850
<b>If he keeps defeating 
players with Unique Stars,</b>

01:30.560 --> 01:32.110
<b>Shinohara Hiroto</b>

01:33.850 --> 01:37.860
<b>he'll eventually become 
an "all-color" Seven Star.</b>

01:38.120 --> 01:42.570
<b>He's played four, won four, and two of those 
were against the Empress and the Phoenix.</b>

01:41.120 --> 01:42.580
<b>Name</b>

01:41.120 --> 01:42.580
<b>Saionji Sarasa</b>

01:41.120 --> 01:42.580
<b>Total Score</b>

01:41.370 --> 01:42.580
<b>LOSER</b>

01:41.370 --> 01:42.580
<b>LOSER</b>

01:42.570 --> 01:45.840
<b>He demonstrated his skills in 
the Self-Made 27-Form Game.</b>

01:45.840 --> 01:50.500
<b>He wielded those exploits with exceptional
 versatility, wit, and imagination.</b>

01:46.950 --> 01:47.920
<b><i>of cards, the reveal phase ends</i></b>

01:46.950 --> 01:47.920
<b><i>and the player with more round points becomes 
the victor of the Self-Made 27-Form Game.</i></b>

01:46.960 --> 01:47.290
<b><i>If both sides run out</i></b>

01:46.960 --> 01:47.290
<b><i>If both sides run out</i></b>

01:46.960 --> 01:47.920
<b><i>Conditions to End the Reveal Phase</i></b>

01:47.290 --> 01:47.920
<b><i>If either side runs out</i></b>

01:47.290 --> 01:47.920
<b><i>If either side runs out</i></b>

01:50.500 --> 01:55.510
<b>Were you aware he had such skills when 
you brought my master to Academy Island?</b>

01:55.510 --> 01:57.100
<b>What do you think?</b>

01:57.100 --> 02:01.020
<b>Well, it was at least obvious he was worth
 more than his transfer exam scores showed.</b>

02:01.450 --> 02:03.970
<b>"Worth"? Are you trying to use my master?</b>

02:03.970 --> 02:08.650
<b>Oh, certainly. I am using him
 to fulfill my own ambitions.</b>

02:08.650 --> 02:11.250
<b>Shinohara must already
 realize that himself.</b>

02:11.250 --> 02:13.080
<b>We're using each other, you see.</b>

02:13.080 --> 02:17.970
<b>Shinohara has a reason to stay on this island, 
and I have my own reasons for needing him.</b>

02:17.970 --> 02:20.500
<b>See? Our interests overlap.</b>

02:20.840 --> 02:22.920
<b>You're using each other?</b>

02:22.920 --> 02:26.060
<b>However, things may not 
go this smoothly forever.</b>

02:26.060 --> 02:29.510
<b>If he keeps gaining stars, 
he'll face greater and greater danger.</b>

02:29.510 --> 02:32.450
<b>And when that happens, what will you do?</b>

02:33.400 --> 02:35.490
<b>You need not worry about that.</b>

02:35.490 --> 02:39.590
<b>I will stay by my master's side,
 no matter what happens.</b>

04:12.640 --> 04:17.650
<b>Chocolate 
and the Devil</b>

04:15.810 --> 04:17.680
<b>My name is Himeji Shirayuki.</b>

04:17.930 --> 04:22.070
<b>Until very recently, I was enrolled 
in Ouka Academy in District 3,</b>

04:22.070 --> 04:25.960
<b>but due to circumstances, 
I have been transferred to Eimei Academy.</b>

04:28.310 --> 04:32.820
<b>I am shy around new people and 
I especially have trouble talking to boys,</b>

04:32.820 --> 04:35.460
<b>so I apologize if I appear rude at times,</b>

04:35.460 --> 04:38.580
<b>but I assure you, 
it does not mean I dislike you.</b>

04:38.580 --> 04:41.090
<b>I would be grateful if 
you could be patient with me.</b>

04:43.590 --> 04:45.400
<b>Whoa.</b>

04:43.590 --> 04:45.970
<b>Himeji Shirayuki</b>

04:44.770 --> 04:45.970
<b>She's so cute!</b>

04:46.520 --> 04:48.470
<b>All right, settle down.</b>

04:49.400 --> 04:52.520
<b>I have one more announcement to make today.</b>

04:52.520 --> 04:55.510
<b>It's about Eimei Academy's 
traditional campus competition event.</b>

04:56.520 --> 05:01.940
<b>8:00 am — 5:00 pm</b>

04:56.520 --> 05:01.940
<b>All students are 
required to participate</b>

04:56.520 --> 05:01.940
<b>All-Campus Elimination Battle</b>

04:56.520 --> 05:01.940
<b>April 25 (Mon) —
April 29 (Fri)</b>

04:56.530 --> 04:59.830
<b>The All-Campus Elimination 
Battle begins next week.</b>

04:59.830 --> 05:06.170
<b>All students will participate in mock games
 using the special Trial command.</b>

05:06.170 --> 05:09.840
<b>In Trial games, Stars will not be exchanged.</b>

05:09.840 --> 05:14.320
<b>Also, you can challenge 
anyone, regardless of rank.</b>

05:14.320 --> 05:16.760
<b>However, if you lose, you're out.</b>

05:16.760 --> 05:20.030
<b>It's a survival contest that ends 
when only one is left standing.</b>

05:20.500 --> 05:25.850
<b>The event will also decide who competes
 in the inter-academy contest next month.</b>

05:25.850 --> 05:30.080
<b>The top five players will 
be chosen to participate.</b>

05:30.330 --> 05:34.280
<b>Whoever lasts the longest 
will also get a wonderful reward,</b>

05:34.280 --> 05:35.500
<b>so give it your best shot!</b>

05:36.530 --> 05:39.070
<b>Here. This one's for you, Himeji.</b>

05:39.320 --> 05:41.440
<b>Is it really all right to accept this?</b>

05:41.440 --> 05:44.490
<b>After you worked so hard to 
acquire this rare chocolate cornet?</b>

05:44.490 --> 05:49.700
<b>Totally. After all, it was thanks to your 
exploits that I beat that guy.</b>

05:54.310 --> 05:58.030
<b>Hey, are you okay? 
You don't need to eat in such a rush.</b>

05:58.030 --> 06:01.970
<b>Oh! Excuse me. It is so delicious, 
I could not help myself.</b>

06:03.470 --> 06:06.260
<b>The All-Campus Elimination
 Battle. In all honesty,</b>

06:06.260 --> 06:09.730
<b>it is full of elements that will be 
very disadvantageous to you, Master.</b>

06:10.000 --> 06:13.460
<b>This event works on a principle 
called "State of Conflict."</b>

06:13.720 --> 06:17.330
<b>You approach the opponent you want 
to challenge and make a Trial request.</b>

06:18.090 --> 06:20.140
<b>The request is accepted automatically,</b>

06:20.140 --> 06:24.670
<b>and you cannot send or receive 
other requests until a winner is decided.</b>

06:21.520 --> 06:26.610
<b>State of Conflict</b>

06:24.670 --> 06:26.610
<b>That is the State of Conflict.</b>

06:26.610 --> 06:32.300
<b>Also, if the State of Conflict continues 
for 24 hours without a Trial taking place,</b>

06:32.300 --> 06:34.250
<b>you will be eliminated.</b>

06:34.950 --> 06:39.200
<b>Even though no Stars are exchanged 
in this event, you still must not lose.</b>

06:40.250 --> 06:44.540
<b>We should devise a strategy that will 
secure your position as the strongest player.</b>

06:44.850 --> 06:47.830
<b>It sounds like just running away 
would be the best move here.</b>

06:47.830 --> 06:52.850
<b>Yes. If you can maintain a minimum distance
 from others, requests cannot be accepted.</b>

06:53.550 --> 06:55.630
<b><i>Hiro-kyun, I think someone's coming!</i></b>

06:57.830 --> 06:58.940
<b>You're Hiroto-kun.</b>

07:00.710 --> 07:01.930
<b>Right?</b>

07:03.690 --> 07:05.440
<b><i>Oh, man!</i></b>

07:05.440 --> 07:09.190
<b><i>She's really pretty, but also looks 
kind of innocent. Like a small animal.</i></b>

07:09.580 --> 07:11.980
<b><i>And those ponytails suit her perfectly.</i></b>

07:12.350 --> 07:16.400
<b>Hm? Hey, Hiroto-kun, are you ignoring me?</b>

07:16.400 --> 07:20.740
<b>When a girl this cute starts talking 
to you, isn't that kind of mean?</b>

07:21.180 --> 07:23.500
<b>Oh, uh, I wasn't trying to ignore you.</b>

07:23.500 --> 07:26.640
<b>Really? Then you must've 
been enchanted by my looks.</b>

07:26.640 --> 07:28.700
<b>I guess I can't blame you!</b>

07:29.000 --> 07:31.000
<b>So, who are you anyway?</b>

07:31.290 --> 07:36.270
<b>Me? I'm Noa. Akizuki Noa.
 Nice to meet you!</b>

07:36.270 --> 07:38.790
<b>I'm a little smaller than everyone else,</b>

07:38.790 --> 07:41.860
<b>but I'm a third-year, 
which means I'm your senpai.</b>

07:42.130 --> 07:44.640
<b>Anyway...</b>

07:46.410 --> 07:49.030
<b>You really are strong, Hiroto-kun.</b>

07:49.290 --> 07:52.740
<b>Hey, you won a battle for the cornets, too!</b>

07:53.830 --> 07:58.830
<b>Yup! Because I'm so strong, smart, and cute!</b>

07:58.830 --> 08:01.490
<b>Ahem. So what did you want?</b>

08:02.590 --> 08:05.030
<b>"Want"? Hm, what do I want?</b>

08:05.030 --> 08:08.620
<b>Well, I guess there is something.</b>

08:08.620 --> 08:11.760
<b>So, are you two going out or what?</b>

08:11.760 --> 08:13.600
<b>Me and Himeji, you mean?</b>

08:13.600 --> 08:15.550
<b>If so, you've got the wrong idea.</b>

08:15.550 --> 08:19.400
<b>At least for the time being, we are 
maintaining a wholesome relationship.</b>

08:19.400 --> 08:22.640
<b>Huh. Okay. I guess not, then.</b>

08:22.640 --> 08:24.390
<b>In that case...</b>

08:24.390 --> 08:25.890
<b>Yay!</b>

08:26.120 --> 08:26.840
<b>Huh?</b>

08:27.450 --> 08:29.560
<b>Hey, get off me.</b>

08:29.560 --> 08:31.070
<b>Huh? Why?</b>

08:31.070 --> 08:34.530
<b>This is your chance to snuggle 
with someone as cute as me!</b>

08:34.530 --> 08:36.710
<b><i>Ah! She smells so sweet!</i></b>

08:37.410 --> 08:38.110
<b>Ow!</b>

08:39.370 --> 08:41.270
<b>Get to the point, Akizuki.</b>

08:41.270 --> 08:44.270
<b>Jeez, you're so pushy, Hiroto-kun.</b>

08:44.270 --> 08:46.030
<b>Fine, I will.</b>

08:46.030 --> 08:48.370
<b>It's about the All-Campus 
Elimination Battle.</b>

08:48.370 --> 08:53.510
<b>Libra did a survey on it. Who you want to 
do a Trial with the most, that kinda thing.</b>

08:53.760 --> 08:58.560
<b>And well, I'm so strong and cute, 
I was naturally near the top of the list,</b>

08:58.560 --> 09:01.270
<b>but it looks like you're by far
the most popular, Hiroto-kun.</b>

09:01.270 --> 09:02.380
<b>Did you know?</b>

09:02.380 --> 09:04.750
<b>No, I hadn't heard.</b>

09:04.750 --> 09:08.280
<b>Huh. You don't look too interested.</b>

09:08.280 --> 09:11.010
<b>I see. I guess that makes sense.</b>

09:12.650 --> 09:14.290
<b>Well, that's about all.</b>

09:14.980 --> 09:17.330
<b>All right. Bye-bye, Hiroto-kun.</b>

09:17.330 --> 09:20.210
<b>Thanks so much for chatting with me!</b>

09:22.120 --> 09:24.200
<b>Keep your guard up around her.</b>

09:24.430 --> 09:27.460
<b>Akizuki Noa-sama, 
nicknamed the Little Devil.</b>

09:27.700 --> 09:31.250
<b>She's one of only three 
Six Star students at Eimei.</b>

09:31.250 --> 09:34.470
<b>A Six Star? Seriously? 
She's really that strong?</b>

09:32.130 --> 09:34.470
<b>Six Stars</b>

09:34.470 --> 09:39.260
<b>Yes. But in addition to that, 
I am getting a very bad feeling about her.</b>

09:39.260 --> 09:41.380
<b>Something monstrous. I am unsure what.</b>

09:43.090 --> 09:47.560
<b>By the way, Master, 
is that the type of girl you are into?</b>

09:47.560 --> 09:47.990
<b>Huh?</b>

09:51.980 --> 09:54.740
<b>District 4</b>

09:51.980 --> 09:54.740
<b>Ichinose Natsume</b>

09:55.040 --> 09:57.850
<b>My, my. This has been difficult.</b>

09:58.520 --> 10:00.800
<b>In that critical game against Kugasaki,</b>

10:00.800 --> 10:04.750
<b>in order to save you, Shirayuki 
had to expose herself to the masses.</b>

10:05.180 --> 10:09.210
<b>Yet on Academy Island, it's unthinkable to be
 supported by a student from another District.</b>

10:09.210 --> 10:13.160
<b>In order to smooth things over, 
I had to transfer her to Eimei.</b>

10:13.940 --> 10:18.940
<b>It was also necessary to recruit her to help
you win the All-Campus Elimination Battle.</b>

10:19.520 --> 10:24.570
<b>Do you realize how troublesome it is 
to transfer a student on Academy Island?</b>

10:24.570 --> 10:27.900
<b>Thanks to you, I got into a lot of trouble.</b>

10:28.180 --> 10:31.530
<b>Does that mean you're going to 
make me do something for you in return?</b>

10:31.770 --> 10:35.900
<b>You're quite perceptive. I don't 
dislike that part of you, Shinohara.</b>

10:36.600 --> 10:41.590
<b>At the present moment, there are two 
very curious things happening on campus.</b>

10:41.840 --> 10:47.140
<b>The first involves outside forces sticking
 their noses into the upcoming event.</b>

10:47.140 --> 10:50.550
<b>They've been setting off alerts 
here and there since yesterday.</b>

10:50.880 --> 10:53.420
<b>What could they be after?</b>

10:53.420 --> 10:57.500
<b>It seems you, the Seven Star, 
are their most likely target.</b>

10:57.500 --> 10:59.420
<b>You're in a very enviable position.</b>

10:59.420 --> 11:02.920
<b>I see. So what's the other thing?</b>

11:03.800 --> 11:08.190
<b>This one is even more troublesome. 
It has to do with the Unique Stars.</b>

11:08.540 --> 11:12.180
<b>Each campus on Academy Island 
is issued one Unique Star.</b>

11:12.530 --> 11:16.320
<b>Eimei had one, too. The Green Unique Star.</b>

11:16.320 --> 11:17.300
<b>"Had"?</b>

11:17.300 --> 11:19.450
<b>Yes. It was stolen.</b>

11:18.030 --> 11:19.740
<b><b>Robbery</b></b>

11:18.030 --> 11:19.740
<b><b>Robbery</b></b>

11:18.030 --> 11:19.740
<b><b>Robbery</b></b>

11:23.030 --> 11:27.940
<b>We were moving its save location to use it as
a prize in the All-Campus Elimination Battle</b>

11:27.940 --> 11:30.360
<b>when it was seemingly taken in a hack.</b>

11:27.950 --> 11:30.210
<b><b>Server Failure</b></b>

11:27.950 --> 11:30.210
<b><b>Server Failure</b></b>

11:27.950 --> 11:30.210
<b><b>Server Failure</b></b>

11:30.360 --> 11:34.820
<b>The Green Star. It definitely has 
some kind of effect on perception,</b>

11:34.820 --> 11:38.210
<b>but the abilities it grants differ 
greatly depending on the person.</b>

11:38.560 --> 11:42.220
<b>If it's in the hands of someone
 who had enough skill to steal it,</b>

11:42.220 --> 11:44.210
<b>who knows what might happen?</b>

11:44.600 --> 11:49.470
<b>The outsider attacks are one thing, but whoever
took the Unique Star must be a student, right?</b>

11:49.470 --> 11:51.970
<b>It isn't clear yet if the 
attacks are connected,</b>

11:51.970 --> 11:54.970
<b>but there's a definite possibility
 it's the same person.</b>

11:55.460 --> 11:58.980
<b>I'd like you to help us 
to root out the culprit.</b>

11:59.330 --> 12:02.730
<b>They will probably take advantage 
of the event to come after you.</b>

12:02.730 --> 12:07.240
<b>So as long as you stay alive in the game, 
they should make the first move.</b>

12:07.910 --> 12:13.600
<b>And remember what I just told you? 
The culprit holds a Unique Star.</b>

12:13.600 --> 12:19.250
<b>The Green Star, which you were supposed 
to win in the All-Campus Elimination Battle.</b>

12:19.510 --> 12:23.450
<b>You must have some idea 
what that means, yes?</b>

12:23.450 --> 12:25.880
<b>You're telling me to get it back myself?</b>

12:27.510 --> 12:31.400
<b>As such, you have three 
missions during this event.</b>

12:31.390 --> 12:36.150
<b><i>Find the 
Culprit</i></b>

12:31.400 --> 12:36.140
<b>Expose the identity of whoever's trying to 
infiltrate the All-Campus Elimination Battle.</b>

12:45.660 --> 12:48.910
<b><i>Recover
 the</i></b>

12:45.660 --> 12:48.910
<b><i>Unique
Star</i></b>

12:45.910 --> 12:48.920
<b>Recover the stolen Unique Star.</b>

13:02.060 --> 13:03.140
<b>And lastly...</b>

13:03.130 --> 13:06.390
<b><i>The Strongest
 on Academy Island</i></b>

13:03.140 --> 13:08.550
<b>Score a decisive victory and clinch the 
position of strongest on Academy Island.</b>

13:10.390 --> 13:11.100
<b>Tch.</b>

13:14.620 --> 13:16.040
<b>They left.</b>

13:16.040 --> 13:19.900
<b>This is gonna be harder than I thought.
 They chase me wherever I go.</b>

13:19.900 --> 13:24.790
<b>The thought of a no-risk game against 
a Seven Star must be very appealing.</b>

13:25.840 --> 13:30.120
<b>Indeed, at the moment, I believe 
we have no other strategy, Master.</b>

13:30.440 --> 13:33.910
<b>We must disable their ability 
to see all participants' locations,</b>

13:33.910 --> 13:38.060
<b>and temporarily block Trial requests 
with some kind of basic jamming</b>

13:38.060 --> 13:39.500
<b>so you can hide from them.</b>

13:41.010 --> 13:44.060
<b>In short, you have to keep running away.</b>

13:47.730 --> 13:51.100
<b>If we can get through this extracurricular 
lesson, the first day is over.</b>

13:51.100 --> 13:53.100
<b>Just a little longer, Master.</b>

13:53.890 --> 13:54.790
<b>Yeah.</b>

14:05.610 --> 14:08.610
<b>Message from Akizuki Noa</b>

14:08.980 --> 14:09.850
<b>Huh?</b>

14:10.490 --> 14:11.970
<b>The jamming didn't work!</b>

14:12.610 --> 14:13.840
<b>Shinohara-kun!</b>

14:14.530 --> 14:16.740
<b>Please play a Trial game with me!</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:22.170
<b>Akizuki Noa</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:22.170
<b>Tee-hee-hee.</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:22.170
<b>Never mind</b>

14:20.030 --> 14:21.850
<b><i>Did she target me directly?</i></b>

14:22.550 --> 14:25.690
<b><i>Has this Akizuki girl 
seen through our strategy?</i></b>

14:25.690 --> 14:27.310
<b>Shinohara-kun?</b>

14:28.490 --> 14:31.940
<b>Yeah, I guess I have to, 
since you asked.</b>

14:32.810 --> 14:35.800
<b>But don't come crying to me when you lose.</b>

14:37.030 --> 14:40.050
<b>Ugh. Tatara was really tough.</b>

14:40.590 --> 14:43.950
<b>No wonder she's president 
of 2-A, the top class.</b>

14:45.040 --> 14:50.150
<b>Master, are you certain it was all 
right for me to take my bath first?</b>

14:50.150 --> 14:51.680
<b>It's fine.</b>

14:51.680 --> 14:55.910
<b>If not for that, you'd change into your maid
 uniform all sweaty and go back to working.</b>

14:55.910 --> 14:59.860
<b>I see. Of course, when you 
compel me to take a bath, Master,</b>

14:59.860 --> 15:02.590
<b>it makes you come across 
as a rather seasoned pervert.</b>

15:03.240 --> 15:04.420
<b>Oh, pardon me.</b>

15:04.660 --> 15:09.050
<b>At any rate, the first day is over. 
How did you feel about it, Master?</b>

15:09.340 --> 15:14.150
<b>Well, I'm at least relieved that the Device 
sensor and basic jamming seem to be working.</b>

15:14.150 --> 15:16.420
<b>But since it's an elimination game,</b>

15:16.420 --> 15:19.500
<b>the ones left at the end will be 
the toughest players, like Akizuki.</b>

15:16.430 --> 15:24.060
<b>Akizuki Noa</b>

15:16.430 --> 15:24.060
<b>Tee-hee-hee.</b>

15:16.430 --> 15:24.060
<b>Never mind</b>

15:19.500 --> 15:24.060
<b>Yes. I am doubtful we will be able to 
keep avoiding her until the final day.</b>

15:24.440 --> 15:27.820
<b>For that reason, I have summoned 
the Company's Head of Electronics.</b>

15:28.330 --> 15:30.320
<b>Here I am!</b>

15:30.320 --> 15:34.580
<b>Your big sis, Kagaya,
 brought you a little gift.</b>

15:34.860 --> 15:37.570
<b>Kagaya-san? In the flesh?</b>

15:38.860 --> 15:40.820
<b><i>Sh-She looks scruffy, but what a babe!</i></b>

15:42.840 --> 15:43.580
<b>How 'bout it?</b>

15:43.870 --> 15:47.840
<b>That logo. Is this from 
that new shop in District 17?</b>

15:48.560 --> 15:52.850
<b>Kagaya-san. What were you doing 
while we were in deep trouble?</b>

15:52.850 --> 15:55.710
<b>Gulp! D-Don't get the wrong idea!</b>

15:56.060 --> 16:01.090
<b>I mean, I was still, like, doing support 
and programming while waiting in line.</b>

16:01.090 --> 16:02.870
<b>That's fine, right?</b>

16:02.870 --> 16:04.220
<b>I never said otherwise.</b>

16:04.430 --> 16:08.230
<b>However, I fail to see why 
you had to go all alone.</b>

16:08.230 --> 16:12.200
<b>Huh? So you're not mad, 
Shirayuki-chan? But you <i>are</i> pouting.</b>

16:12.200 --> 16:13.740
<b>I am not pouting.</b>

16:13.740 --> 16:15.290
<b>Huh? Huh? Huh?</b>

16:15.290 --> 16:19.240
<b>Hey, are you seeing this, Hiro-kyun? 
Isn't she acting, like, super cute?</b>

16:19.240 --> 16:21.120
<b>I-I am not acting cute!</b>

16:21.350 --> 16:23.860
<b>Aw, Shirayuki-chan. My bad, my bad!</b>

16:23.860 --> 16:26.470
<b>I'll feed one to you. Open up and say "aah"!</b>

16:26.470 --> 16:30.750
<b>Huh? But... I cannot do that
 with my master watching.</b>

16:30.750 --> 16:34.000
<b>It'll turn Hiro-kyun on, so don't sweat it!</b>

16:34.000 --> 16:35.500
<b>See? Here!</b>

16:37.090 --> 16:41.760
<b>You always have such pretty hair. Like, swoon.</b>

16:41.760 --> 16:44.620
<b>K-Kagaya-san! Is that what you came here for?</b>

16:44.620 --> 16:48.770
<b>Oh, yeah, right. I came to 
explain something to you.</b>

16:49.210 --> 16:53.850
<b>I figured it'd be tough for you to run away
 using the programs we already have,</b>

16:53.850 --> 16:59.040
<b>so I wrote a new Device ability for 
all the worrywart Hiro-kyuns out there.</b>

16:59.040 --> 17:02.550
<b>I'll overlap Hiro-kyun's location 
data with Shirayuki-chan's.</b>

17:02.550 --> 17:06.490
<b>And any requests Hiro-kyun receives 
will go to Shirayuki-chan's Device.</b>

17:06.490 --> 17:09.050
<b>So, basically, she'll accept them instead!</b>

17:09.050 --> 17:11.420
<b>I call it the Scapegoat Technique!</b>

17:13.260 --> 17:16.500
<b>This should at least buy you a few days.</b>

17:16.500 --> 17:20.030
<b>If it comes down to it,
there is a way to emergency bail, too,</b>

17:20.030 --> 17:22.420
<b>but you can only use that once.</b>

17:22.420 --> 17:25.670
<b>Yeah, but are you okay with it, Himeji?</b>

17:26.020 --> 17:30.430
<b>If this helps you in some way, 
Master, I am very happy to do it.</b>

17:30.430 --> 17:34.390
<b>O-Oh, yeah? Then, sure. I guess it's okay.</b>

17:41.760 --> 17:46.610
<b><i>Looks like I don't have to worry. 
In that case, I have only one job.</i></b>

17:46.990 --> 17:48.660
<b><i>I just have to run!</i></b>

17:56.550 --> 17:57.480
<b>Who's there?</b>

18:03.920 --> 18:05.570
<b><i>We are in trouble, Master!</i></b>

18:05.570 --> 18:07.640
<b><i>I received a transmission from Kagaya-san.</i></b>

18:07.640 --> 18:13.030
<b><i>She said the All-Campus Elimination Battle 
survivors are closing in on your location.</i></b>

18:13.030 --> 18:14.450
<b><i>There's 200 of them!</i></b>

18:14.450 --> 18:15.900
<b>What are you saying?</b>

18:15.900 --> 18:19.090
<b><i>Your coordinates were sent to
 everyone simultaneously, Master!</i></b>

18:19.090 --> 18:21.150
<b><i>Leave that area right away!</i></b>

18:21.150 --> 18:22.160
<b>Right!</b>

18:33.320 --> 18:36.640
<b><i>But why? There was no signal a second ago!</i></b>

18:36.640 --> 18:39.390
<b>I guess I bumped into you again, Hiroto-kun.</b>

18:39.790 --> 18:41.890
<b>Akizuki? But why?</b>

18:44.820 --> 18:46.050
<b>Master!</b>

18:51.500 --> 18:56.250
<b>You really shouldn't. I know I'm so cute
 you'd want to have your way with me,</b>

18:56.250 --> 18:58.650
<b>but I don't like people who use force.</b>

18:58.920 --> 19:01.580
<b>Then let me go!</b>

19:01.580 --> 19:04.440
<b>No way! What are you talking about?</b>

19:04.440 --> 19:10.070
<b>I'm just stuck because you've pushed
me down and gotten on top of me.</b>

19:10.610 --> 19:13.500
<b>You can't run away now, can you?</b>

19:18.390 --> 19:20.210
<b>Send a Trial request, Himeji!</b>

19:20.800 --> 19:21.920
<b>O-Okay!</b>

19:27.680 --> 19:30.150
<b>Aw, too bad!</b>

19:30.150 --> 19:35.060
<b>And right when we were about 
to become a big news scandal.</b>

19:35.320 --> 19:40.580
<b>Oh well. At least I achieved 
my number one goal. I guess that's enough.</b>

19:41.310 --> 19:43.430
<b>All right, see you later, Hiroto-kun!</b>

19:43.820 --> 19:46.830
<b>Wait, Akizuki! What goal do you mean?</b>

19:49.420 --> 19:53.220
<b>I'm just too cute and silly. How would I know?</b>

19:55.040 --> 19:57.260
<b>I am sorry I could not help.</b>

19:57.720 --> 19:59.560
<b>What are you talking about, Himeji?</b>

19:59.560 --> 20:01.850
<b>I'm safe, thanks to you.</b>

20:01.850 --> 20:04.420
<b>Thank you very much, Master.</b>

20:05.480 --> 20:08.170
<b><i>What was she after, anyway?</i></b>

20:11.630 --> 20:13.910
<b>Uh, what's this?</b>

20:14.270 --> 20:15.340
<b>A cutlet.</b>

20:15.660 --> 20:20.660
<b>I put my maid's heart and soul into it,
hoping it aids you to be a cut above the rest.</b>

20:23.360 --> 20:24.400
<b>Thank you.</b>

20:24.720 --> 20:26.430
<b>I shall prepare it now.</b>

20:28.720 --> 20:29.670
<b>What's wrong?</b>

20:30.710 --> 20:32.910
<b>We have no cutlet sauce.</b>

20:32.910 --> 20:37.580
<b>Oh. Yeah, we might be out. We should
 still have Worcestershire sauce, though?</b>

20:37.580 --> 20:40.890
<b>No. You and I are both on 
Team Cutlet Sauce, Master.</b>

20:40.890 --> 20:43.170
<b>My pride will not allow me 
to compromise on sauce.</b>

20:43.800 --> 20:45.400
<b>I shall go to the store.</b>

20:45.400 --> 20:46.640
<b>Why don't I go instead?</b>

20:46.640 --> 20:49.590
<b>You cannot. It would tarnish my reputation.</b>

20:55.660 --> 20:58.100
<b><i>So Himeji went out, just like that...</i></b>

21:02.490 --> 21:03.740
<b>Something's not right.</b>

21:07.120 --> 21:07.740
<b>Himeji Shirayuki</b>

21:08.430 --> 21:09.490
<b>Hello?</b>

21:09.490 --> 21:12.740
<b><i>Hiya, Hiroto-kun. Having a good night?</i></b>

21:12.740 --> 21:15.510
<b>Hey. What the hell do 
you think you're doing?</b>

21:15.510 --> 21:17.190
<b>Huh? What do you mean?</b>

21:17.190 --> 21:20.260
<b>I just bumped into your little "maid-chan."</b>

21:20.510 --> 21:22.500
<b>You'd better not have 
done anything to Himeji.</b>

21:22.500 --> 21:24.900
<b>Jeez, you have such a short temper.</b>

21:25.340 --> 21:27.760
<b>Fine. I'll put her on.</b>

21:28.080 --> 21:31.380
<b>Your precious, precious little "maid-chan."</b>

21:31.640 --> 21:32.500
<b>Himeji?</b>

21:33.470 --> 21:34.890
<b>Master...</b>

21:35.120 --> 21:39.140
<b><i>I beg your pardon. I will not 
be able to return home today.</i></b>

21:39.140 --> 21:41.610
<b>You can't come home? 
Did she do something to you?</b>

21:42.000 --> 21:44.490
<b><i>Forgive me. I cannot say that, either.</i></b>

21:45.520 --> 21:50.530
<b>Master, in order to shut out 
Trial requests from others,</b>

21:50.530 --> 21:54.410
<b>you and I are now in a 
temporary State of Conflict.</b>

21:54.930 --> 21:55.810
<b>Right.</b>

21:55.810 --> 21:56.910
<b><i>And, well...</i></b>

21:57.820 --> 21:58.980
<b>About that...</b>

21:59.660 --> 22:03.660
<b>I am no longer able to 
lose our game tomorrow.</b>
